<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Converting radians to degrees</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>An angle \(\theta\) is given in radians:</p>
\[ \theta = {@trad@}. \]
<p>Convert \(\theta\) to degrees. Give your answer as a whole number.</p>
<div>\(\theta = \) [[input:ans1]]\(^\circ\) [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>
<p><strong>Step 1: use the conversion fact.</strong> A half-turn is \(\pi\) radians, which is \(180^\circ\):</p>
\[ \pi \text{ radians} = 180^\circ, \qquad\text{so}\qquad 1 \text{ radian} = \frac{180^\circ}{\pi}. \]

<p><strong>Step 2: multiply by \(\dfrac{180^\circ}{\pi}\).</strong> To change radians to degrees, multiply the angle by \(\dfrac{180^\circ}{\pi}\):</p>
\[ \theta = {@trad@} \times \frac{180^\circ}{\pi}. \]

<p><strong>Step 3: cancel \(\pi\) and simplify.</strong> The \(\pi\) on the top cancels with the \(\pi\) on the bottom, leaving</p>
\[ \theta = \frac{[[if test="is(pp>1)"]]{@pp@} \times [[/if]]180^\circ}{{@qq@}}[[if test="is(pp>1)"]] = {@pp@} \times {@unit@}^\circ[[/if]] = {@ta@}^\circ. \]
<p>[[if test="is(pp>1)"]]It is easiest to divide \(180\) by \({@qq@}\) first, giving \({@unit@}\), and then multiply by \({@pp@}\).[[else]]Dividing \(180\) by \({@qq@}\) gives \({@ta@}\).[[/if]]</p>
<div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="Circle showing the angle {#ta#} degrees measured anticlockwise from the positive x-axis.">
[[jsxgraph width="300px" height="300px"]]
(function() {
  var A = {#ta#}, num = {#pp#}, den = {#qq#};
  var b = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[-1.5, 1.5, 1.5, -1.5], axis:false, grid:false,
      keepaspectratio:true, showNavigation:false, showCopyright:false});
  b.create('arrow', [[-1.4, 0], [1.45, 0]], {strokeColor:'#444', fixed:true, highlight:false});
  b.create('arrow', [[0, -1.4], [0, 1.45]], {strokeColor:'#444', fixed:true, highlight:false});
  b.create('circle', [[0, 0], 1], {strokeColor:'#90a4ae', strokeWidth:1.5, fixed:true, highlight:false});
  var O = b.create('point', [0, 0], {visible:false, fixed:true});
  var X = b.create('point', [1, 0], {visible:false, fixed:true});
  var r = A*Math.PI/180;
  var P = b.create('point', [Math.cos(r), Math.sin(r)], {name:'', size:3, color:'#c62828', fixed:true});
  b.create('segment', [O, X], {strokeColor:'#c62828', strokeWidth:2, fixed:true});
  b.create('segment', [O, P], {strokeColor:'#c62828', strokeWidth:2, fixed:true});
  var lab = (num === 1 ? '' : num) + 'π/' + den + ' = ' + A + '°';
  b.create('angle', [X, O, P], {radius:0.35, name:lab, fillColor:'#ffb74d', fillOpacity:0.35,
      strokeColor:'#ef6c00', fixed:true, label:{color:'#ef6c00', fontSize:13}});
})();
[[/jsxgraph]]
</div>
<p><strong>Final answer:</strong> \({@trad@}\) radians \(= {@ta@}^\circ\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
